<title>
Shift Lock Solenoid Inspection
</title>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A5106012001">
<title>
Function Check
</title>
<ptxt>
When ignition is “ON” with brake pedal depressed, select lever button (1) can be pushed and select lever can be shifted from P range.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGSB0A510035.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "52.960mm" ver = "01" gw = "198" gh = "134"/>
</figure>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A5106012002">
<title>
Operation Check
</title>
<attention4>
<ptxt>
Short circuit or an improper connection will damage the shift lock solenoid.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Check that the power supply voltage and test connections are both correct.
</ptxt>
</attention4>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove floor console box. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A9806020"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Disconnect select lever connector (1).
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check that shift lock solenoid rod moves smoothly and then returns when positive terminal of battery is connected to terminal “5” and negative (–) terminal of battery is connected to terminal “10”.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If solenoid rod does not move smoothly, replace select lever.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IDAA0A550036.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "93.592mm" ver = "01" gw = "195" gh = "249"/>
</figure>
